Abstraction

The 8-Puzzle can be represented as a state-space search problem.

Initial State

+---+---+---+
| 1 | 2 | 3 |
+---+---+---+
| 4 |   | 6 |
+---+---+---+
| 7 | 5 | 8 |
+---+---+---+

Goal State

+---+---+---+
| 1 | 2 | 3 |
+---+---+---+
| 4 | 5 | 6 |
+---+---+---+
| 7 | 8 |   |
+---+---+---+

The main components are:

- State: Arrangement of tiles on the board.
- Initial State: Starting arrangement.
- Goal State: Required final arrangement.
- Operators: Moving the blank space up, down, left, or right.
- Path Cost: Cost of each movement.
- Heuristic: Estimated cost of reaching the goal.

The search process generates possible states and selects the most promising state using the A* evaluation function.
